# The build context is the repository root (the Dockerfiles copy src/ and docs/), and without
# this file every `docker build` shipped the whole working tree to the daemon — 1.3GB of
# node_modules, bin/ and obj/ that no Dockerfile reads, discovered when the self-host boot proof
# crawled (#252). Multi-gigabyte contexts are why local image builds took tens of minutes.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
.git/
.claude/
.telemetry/
**/.vite/
**/dist/
src/root/AiOrchestrator.Server/wwwroot/
